menu "Network OTA (net_ota)"

    config NET_OTA_PORT
        int "HTTP port of the update server"
        default 80
        range 1 65535

    config NET_OTA_MAX_SOCKETS
        int "Max open sockets of the server net_ota starts itself"
        default 2
        range 1 7
        help
            httpd reserves 3 more sockets internally. The default of 2 leaves most of
            LWIP_MAX_SOCKETS for the application's own client connections.

    config NET_OTA_BUF_SIZE
        int "Receive buffer size (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 1024 65536

    config NET_OTA_CONFIRM_TIMEOUT_S
        int "Seconds a new image has to call net_ota_mark_valid()"
        default 120
        range 10 3600
        help
            After an update the new image boots as PENDING_VERIFY. If it has not called
            net_ota_mark_valid() within this time, net_ota restarts the chip and the
            bootloader rolls back to the previous image. Needs
            BOOTLOADER_APP_ROLLBACK_ENABLE.

endmenu
